<title>TURKEY: Turkey natgas consumption up at 7.9 bcm in 1996.</title>
<headline>Turkey natgas consumption up at 7.9 bcm in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's natural gas consumption rose to 7.9 billion cubic metres (bcm) in 1996, up 15.6 percent from the previous year, the Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>It said 7.76 bcm of natural gas was imported in 1996, led by 5.53 bcm of imports from Russia which was slightly below 1995's 5.56 bcm.</p>
<p>Total imports in 1995 were 6.72 bcm.</p>
<p>Domestic natural gas production rose 12.8 percent from a year ago to 205.6 million cubic metres last year, said the Anatolian report based on Energy Ministry data.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
